Values are interpolated with an f-string, so a quote in `sku` breaks the SQL and crafted input changes the query (SQL injection). The table name is also unvalidated.

```python
from psycopg2 import sql

ALLOWED = {"products", "products_archive"}

def get_product(cur, orgid, sku, table):
    if table not in ALLOWED:
        raise ValueError(table)
    q = sql.SQL("SELECT * FROM {} WHERE orgid = %s AND sku = %s").format(sql.Identifier(table))
    cur.execute(q, (orgid, sku))
    return cur.fetchone()
```
The driver now sends values safely escaped; identifiers are quoted by `sql.Identifier` and restricted to an allow-list.
